# Never enable Windows FIPS policy on BEAVIS2

Operator hard rule (Phil, 2026-09-25): **do not switch BEAVIS2 to
Windows FIPS mode.** That OS bit breaks required programs on the
operator console. Product cryptography still uses in-process Amazon
Web Services LibCrypto (AWS-LC) Federal Information Processing
Standards (FIPS) (`aws-lc-rs`). That is not the same as the Windows
`FipsAlgorithmPolicy` registry value.

## The rule

> **Leave `HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Lsa\FipsAlgorithmPolicy`
> `Enabled=0` on BEAVIS2 / the operator console. Never set `Enabled=1`
> as a "fix" for rustls, AWS-LC, or a configurator crash. Do not run
> Workstation Assurance (WA) / Current State Compliance (CSC) Fix-It
> `win.fips-algorithm-policy` with confirm on this host. Analog
> Informatics Corporation (AIC) programs must launch whether that OS
> bit is 0 or 1 -- do not gate launch on the OS policy.**

## Two different FIPS surfaces

| Surface | Where | On BEAVIS2 |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Windows `FipsAlgorithmPolicy` | `HKLM\...\Lsa\FipsAlgorithmPolicy` | **Enabled=0**. Never turn on. |
| Product AWS-LC FIPS | in-process `aws-lc-rs` / rustls | Required. Not the OS policy. |

## Forbidden

- `Set-ItemProperty` / Fix-It apply that writes `Enabled=1` on Beavis2
- Treating OS FIPS off as the root cause of a configurator crash
- Gating `main()` or a desktop shortcut on the OS policy bit
- Enabling OS FIPS to "match" CMVP #4759

## Required

- Prove crashes from logs / Windows Error Reporting (WER), then fix
  the binary (stale EXE, Dynamic Link Library (DLL) sidecar, Event
  Log, rustls provider).
- Customer endpoints may still apply `win.fips-algorithm-policy`. The
  agent refuses that class when the machine name contains `Beavis2`.

## Origin

2026-09-25 -- operator: do not switch BEAVIS2 to Windows FIPS mode;
allow local launch with the OS bit 0 or 1; product FIPS is AWS-LC.
